## Summary
The Trump administration is reportedly preparing to revoke business and tourism visas for up to 200,000 individuals seeking asylum in the US, which is described as the largest visa revocation ever. This action targets visa holders who are asylum seekers and could have significant immigration implications.

## Key Points
- The Trump administration plans to revoke visas on a large scale.
- Up to 200,000 business and tourism visas may be affected.
- The individuals impacted are seeking asylum in the US.
- This is reported as the largest visa revocation in history.
- The action is based on media reports and involves asylum-related immigration policies.


